d": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le16ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hello. I'm here to get a pass.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: A visitors' pass? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Maybe. She told me I needed to get a pass before my meet and greet.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Which office? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Cambridge Life. They hired me.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: You need an access card. Can I get your name please?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sally. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: I'm sorry. What was that? Molly?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No, Sally.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Is \"Sally\" spelled with a Y or an IE at the end?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: A Y. <br/>", "id": 1, "time": "10", "image": "engenn5le16ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Sorry. What did you say your name was?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sally Davis.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: What's your address?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: 4523 Hollyoak Street.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Sorry. I didn't catch the last part.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Number 4523 on Hollyoak Street. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Your date of birth?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: April 20th, 1980.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: I thought I heard the 20th.Is that correct?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, the 20th.<br/>", "id": 2, "time": "34000", "image": "engenn5le16ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Ok. Here you are. You can only use this at the front entrance. If you use the back door, you need to punch in a code. The code is 9-4-0...<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Could you repeat that please?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Clerk</span>: 9-4-0-2.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Thanks.", "id": 3, "time": "64000", "image": "engenn5le16ob05re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally Gets a Job at a Magazine"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "First Day at the Office"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le16ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Irregular Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Past Simple tense to talk about actions that happened in the past.<br/><br/>To form the Past Simple tense of a <span class=\"italic\">regular</span> verb, you follow certain rules.<br/><br/>Some verbs do not follow any rules. They are called <span class=\"italic\">irregular verbs</span>. Here are the past tense forms of some irregular verbs:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes the verb changes completely:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">think</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">thought</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">was</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes there is \\\"half\\\" a change:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">write</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">do</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">wrote</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">did</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes there is no change:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I thought I heard the 20th. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I read that the card was for all new employees. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The receptionist told me to come here. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wrote down the wrong address."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "  If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite <br/><br/>  One way to ask for clarification is to ask the person to repeat what they said.<br/><br/>  Here are some phrases and expressions you can use to ask for repetition or clarification:<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">Excuse me?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you repeat that?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you say that again?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What did you say?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What was that (again)?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Did you say . . . ?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">I'm sorry. I didn't catch that.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Is it X or Y? *</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Is that correct?</span></li> </ul><br/><br/> *<span class=\"italic\">If you want to clarify between two things, you can ask if it's *(X) or (Y)?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm sorry. I'm not quite sure I caught that. Can you repeat that please?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Is Cathy spelled with a C or K? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you say 289?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "visitor's pass"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a small card that is used by someone who doesn't work in a specific building "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will need a visitor's pass. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about entering an office building."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "access card"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a plastic card used to provide access to a building "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am a new employee. I need to get an access card."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "front entrance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the main doors you go through at the front to enter a building "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use this card when you enter through the front entrance. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "back door"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a door at the back or side of a building "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You can use the back door as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to punch in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to push buttons on a machine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to punch in the numbers in the morning."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "code"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of numbers you use to open something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Punch in the code to open the door."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pretend you just started a new job. You are finishing your first day."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 10 - 12 sentences about what happened. What did you do? How did you feel? Who did you meet? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Circle all the verbs in the Simple Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your sentences. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading them aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about actions and events in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about a day at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about actions related to work."}]}], "type": "sena"}